# SA-23, §14.5: ThreadSanitizer reports that are not races in this code base, each with its reason.
#
# tokio's I/O driver hands each socket's ScheduledIo to the kernel with epoll_ctl and gets it back
# from epoll_wait on the driver thread. ThreadSanitizer does not see that kernel round trip as a
# happens-before edge, so every socket a test opens (PostgreSQL, HTTP) shows a race between the
# registration and the driver's readiness update.
race:tokio::runtime::io::scheduled_io
race:tokio::runtime::io::driver
race:tokio::runtime::io::registration_set
